{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b> lest he meet us</b>. They wanted to say פֶּן יִפְגָּעֲךָ (lest he meet you), but they showed honor to the monarchy. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 5:3). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 5:3): <b> lest he meet us</b> includes — we Israelites, you Pharaoh, and all Egypt; therefore when they saw the plague of the firstborn they said, \"we are all dead men\" (Exodus 12:33), for the words of Moses were confirmed to them when he said \"lest he meet us with pestilence,\" so they drove them out to go and slaughter. But this statement of his is not correct, for they were not commanded to say that there would be pestilence or sword among Israel if they did not slaughter, and they would not alter anything in the mission of HaShem. And by way of truth, it is the secret of the sacrifices, that they are an atonement from the פְּגִיעָה (the smiting), for before Him goes pestilence (Habakkuk 3:5) or by His severe sword. He said this because the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded them, \"And you shall say to him: YHWH, the Elohim of the Hebrews, has met with us; and now let us go, we pray, three days' journey into the wilderness, that we may sacrifice to YHWH our Elohim\" (Exodus 3:18), but they said, \"Thus says YHWH, the Elohim of Israel: Let my people go\" (Exodus 5:1). Now Pharaoh was a great sage and knew Elohim and acknowledged Him, as he — or Morish his teacher — said concerning Joseph, \"Since Elohim has made all this known to you\" (Genesis 41:39), \"a man in whom the spirit of Elohim is\" (Genesis 41:38). But he did not know the particular Name, and he answered, \"I do not know YHWH\" (Exodus 5:2). So they remembered and returned and said to him as they were commanded: \"The Elohim of the Hebrews has met with us\" (Exodus 5:3), for they mentioned to him only the Elohim of the Hebrews — that is El Shaddai — and they said \"has met with us\" (נִקְרָה עָלֵינוּ), using the language of מִקְרֶה (meeting) as they were commanded; and they explained to him that in this מִקְרָא (meeting) that had come upon them, they would need to slaughter before Him, lest the פְּגִיעָה (smiting) come with pestilence or with sword. And of the same matter it says concerning Balaam: \"And Elohim met Balaam, and he said to Him: I have arranged the seven altars, and I have offered up a bull and a ram on each altar\" (Numbers 23:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase או מורישו ליוסף (\"or Morish his teacher to Joseph\") is textually uncertain; it may be corrupt. Read hyper-literally as it stands. Ramban apparently raises the possibility that the speaker of the Genesis verses is either Pharaoh or a figure named Morish."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:03:21.286791183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}